{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>If its owner is with it.</b> Whether he is engaged in that same labor or in other labor — if he was with him at the time of the borrowing, he need not be with him at the time of the breakage or death (ibid.)." "<b>If it is a hire.</b> If the animal is not borrowed but hired — it comes under its hire-fee to this hirer, and not as a loan; and not all its benefit is his, for he uses it by means of its hire-fee, and he does not have the legal status of a borrower to be liable for injury; and Scripture did not specify its law — whether like an unpaid bailee or like a paid bailee. Therefore the Sages of Israel disputed how a hirer pays: Rabbi Meir says, like an unpaid bailee; Rabbi Yehudah says, like a paid bailee (Bava Metzi'a 95a)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:54.653788288Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}